  "spec": "SPEC-CONTRACT-SERVER §3.14.1 and §3.14.2, integer math. A case's inputs are `defaults` with its `set` applied. score = clamp(0, 100, base + evidence + review + history + use + tests + anchors + contradiction); then, if public_vault and not author_costly_signal, score = min(score, 39). base: own 60, workspace 55, public 30, foreign 20. evidence: observed 15, imported 5, stated 0. review: person_accept 20, else reviewer_accept (weight >= required) 15, else 0. history: history_events (the writing worker's events in this place with t_ref - 90 days < received_at <= t_ref) < 20 -> 0; history_reverts * 5 > history_events (revert_ratio > 0.20) -> -10; else round(10 * (1 - reverts/events)) with halves rounded up, i.e. (20 * (events - reverts) + events) / (2 * events) in integer division. use: +5 if delivered_at_ms is set and t_ref_ms - delivered_at_ms >= 30 days and contradicts_edges (open or resolved) = 0; +5 if inbound_refs (references + derived_from) >= 3. tests: +5 if fresh_test_refs >= 1. anchors: refs_gone >= 1 -> -20, else refs_to_verify >= 1 -> -10. contradiction: contradicts_open >= 1 -> -15. bucket: high >= 70, normal 40-69, low < 40; trust_pin high or normal overrides the bucket, never the score. t_ref_ms is the evaluation time: received_at of the newest folded event for sealed engines, never the local clock."
